SAVINGS TARGET TRACKER

Savings Target Tracker — a real-world task using only this week's concepts: for loops, range(), looping a fixed number of times, input() inside a loop, adding up totals inside a loop, counting with variables - plus reusing while validation, comparisons, if / elif / else, variables, input(), float(), arithmetic, and printing with 2-decimal money format. No imports, no tricks.

Solve it individually, then come together as a group to compare approaches. Good luck!

A tailoring apprentice on Ojoto Street is saving for her own sewing machine. She saves a different amount every week, so she wants a small program that tracks the weeks one by one and tells her at the end whether she hit her target.

The program must:
- Ask "Saving for how many weeks: " and keep asking until the number is at least 1.
- Ask "Target amount: " (decimals allowed).
- Then, for each week in order, ask "Week 1 savings: " (decimals allowed - a 0 week is allowed and still counts as a week), and after each entry print one line in this shape: Week 2: saved N8000.00 (total so far: N15000.00)
- While looping, also count the STRONG WEEKS - weeks where she saved 10000 or more.
- After the last week, print exactly three lines:
  TOTAL SAVED: N20500.50
  STRONG WEEKS: 1
  GOAL REACHED - extra N500.50   (if the total is at or above the target)
  or
  SHORTFALL: N4999.50   (if the total is below the target)

Sample run:

Saving for how many weeks: 3
Target amount: 20000
Week 1 savings: 8000
Week 1: saved N8000.00 (total so far: N8000.00)
Week 2 savings: 0
Week 2: saved N0.00 (total so far: N8000.00)
Week 3 savings: 12500.50
Week 3: saved N12500.50 (total so far: N20500.50)

TOTAL SAVED: N20500.50
STRONG WEEKS: 1
GOAL REACHED - extra N500.50

Edge cases to handle: a single week (the only week decides everything), an entry of 0 weeks (rejected, asked again), a final total exactly equal to the target (GOAL REACHED, extra N0.00), a zero in the middle of the schedule, every week a strong week, and no week a strong week.
